}}

=== Quantitative Example (Track B) ===

Let <math>m = 0.01</math> (bare mass in natural units), <math>\lambda = 0.1</math>, operator-sustained <math>\psi_0 = 3</math>:

:<math>m_{\rm eff}^2 = (0.01)^2 + 3(0.1)(3)^2 = 0.0001 + 2.7 = 2.7001</math>
:<math>m_{\rm eff} \approx 1.643</math>

The nonlinear term dominates by a factor of 27,000. The coherence length shrinks from <math>L_\psi^{\rm (bare)} = 1/0.01 = 100</math> (in natural units) to <math>L_\psi^{\rm (eff)} = 1/1.643 \approx 0.61</math> — a reduction by factor 164. Without dispersion compensation, a device calibrated to the bare mass would operate far outside its design regime.

